Competitive Landscape
Honeywell International dominates the commercial aircraft APU segment, leveraging long standing supply agreements with leading OEMs and a robust test bed infrastructure. Its portfolio ranges from small turbofan driven units for regional jets to high power models for wide body aircraft, making Honeywell a reference supplier across new airplane programmes.
Beyond Honeywell, Safran and Pratt & Whitney occupy significant market shares with high efficiency units for Airbus platforms and rugged designs suitable for military transport. Rolls Royce and MTU Aero Engines offer derivative models that benefit from their core engine expertise and cater to retrofit programmes. Smaller, specialty manufacturers – such as Meggitt, Hamilton Sundstrand (Collins Aerospace) and United Technologies’ legacy divisions – compete on weight reduction, modularity and niche design capabilities.
